# Implementation Plan — AI-Powered Criminal Network Analysis System (SIH26189)

Targeted for Smart India Hackathon problem statement **SIH26189** (Ministry of Home Affairs / NCRB, Women Safety Division). Ingests multi-source, mixed structured/unstructured case data (FIR text, surveillance reports, social media intel, CDRs, financial transactions), extracts entities, normalizes and builds a relationship graph, ranks key individuals with explainable rationales, flags ML/rule-based anomalies, and visualizes everything via an investigator-facing dashboard with network graph, temporal heatmap, geographic hotspot map, and co-occurrence matrix.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Synthetic / Demo Data**: In strict accordance with the hackathon rules and problem statement guidelines, all data generated and bundled is synthetic demo data and clearly labeled as such in the UI.
> - **Graph Processing Engine**: Following §1 fallback specification, NetworkX in-memory is utilized on the FastAPI backend for fast, deterministic sub-second calculation of PageRank, Betweenness Centrality, and Louvain Community Detection, avoiding heavy Neo4j JVM startup overhead and guaranteeing instant sub-3-second load times during judging.
> - **Pre-cached Demo Mode**: The bundled sample dataset (PDF, CSV, XLSX) is pre-parsed and cached on application startup so clicking "Load Sample Case" populates the entire dashboard in under 1 second.

